
# Python virtual environments
venv/
env/
.venv/

# Python cache files
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo

# Environment variables and secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Git files
.git/
.gitignore

# Jupyter Notebook checkpoints
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# IDE settings
.vscode/
.idea/

# Testing and coverage
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Logs
*.log
logs/

# Operating system files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Docker files
.dockerignore

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.bak

# Documentation (optional)
README.md
docs/

# Local datasets and large files (adjust if required)
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.parquet

# Model training artifacts (adjust if required)
mlruns/
```

### Why these exclusions?

| Folder/File | Reason |
|---|---|
| `venv/` | Avoid copying local Python packages |
| `.env` | Protect environment variables and secrets |
| `.git/` | Reduce Docker build context |
| `__pycache__/` | Exclude unnecessary Python cache |
| `.ipynb_checkpoints/` | Remove notebook temporary files |
| `mlruns/` | Avoid copying MLflow experiment artifacts |
| `*.csv` | Avoid copying large datasets unnecessarily |

**Important for RetailPulse:** If your application needs CSV datasets, trained `.pkl` models, or other files at runtime, do not exclude them. Remove the corresponding patterns from `.dockerignore`.

For example, if your Streamlit application loads a trained model from `deployment/model/`, make sure that directory is included in your Docker image.